WEBVTT

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.480
Setsuna... Setsuna!

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:10.610
I might break.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:23.120
Where am I?

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.210
What happened?

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:29.230
I've heard they're selling robot 
dogs on the mainland now!

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:31.520
What, really? I want one!

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.860
Maybe they'll sell them on the 
island in a couple years or so.

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:36.710
No way. Even if they did, 
you couldn't afford one.

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:39.470
Maybe Karen could buy one.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:42.180
Hey, Karen.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:44.730
Wh-What was the question?

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:49.160
A robot dog.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:52.910
Sorry, I was thinking 
about something I forgot.

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:53.740
I'll be right back!

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:51.170
<b>We Meet Again</b>

00:01:53.800 --> 00:02:00.450
<b>Most Wanted</b>

00:01:53.800 --> 00:02:00.450
<b>People of Interest</b>

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:56.130
That was rather unfortunate, Karen-chan.

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:58.400
I told you not to call me that!

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.640
Right, sorry.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:01.710
I can go, right?

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:02.930
Yeah, thanks.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.100
Take care.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:07.450
I'm here.

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:08.390
Y-Yeah.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:25.070
You have no memory?

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:25.920
Nope!

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:26.800
Not even your name?

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:27.450
Nope!

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:28.910
Do you remember <i>anything?</i>

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:31.420
I'm supposed to save a girl.

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:36.340
<b>Japan Overseas Cooperation Volunteers
Senior Overseas Volunteer</b>

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:34.880
And save the world.

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:41.060
I think I came back in time to do those things.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.050
That's all that I remember!

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:44.460
Give me a break.

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:46.140
Sorry.

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:50.520
And there's... someone...

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:56.530
Someone... I need to kill.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:02:59.900
So, anyway,

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:01.490
is this yours?

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:06.840
I just picked that up to cover my front.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:10.410
Oh, is that girl okay? 
She got quite an eyeful.

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:12.680
I bet she'll take it pretty hard.

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:14.750
She's an innocent high schooler.

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:18.380
"Innocent"? She seemed pretty tough.

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:24.420
Whoa, what am I, a dirty old man?

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:33.230
Once again, a storm has brought 
a mystery along with that island.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:35.690
Island?

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.040
This is Kurutsu.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:51.410
I heard someone's been washed up again.

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:56.240
<i>Yes, he's a young man around 20. 
I was just interviewing him,</i>

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:58.310
<i>but he seems to have lost his memory.</i>

00:03:58.310 --> 00:04:02.660
<i>I thought I should contact headquarters 
and have him stay here until I hear back.</i>

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:03.300
No!

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.300
Outsiders must leave immediately!

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.680
We must expel him in accordance 
with our traditions!

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.730
<b>Urashima Library</b>

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.730
Sorry to do this to you,

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:21.030
but we need to send you to the mainland.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:24.930
Personally, I would've liked 
to have heard about the future.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:27.740
If you really did travel 
through time, that is.

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:36.930
Excuse me...

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:39.840
I want to stay on this island.

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:41.760
Did you remember something?

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:42.700
Not at all.

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:43.630
Geez.

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:48.950
But I think I'm supposed to stay here.

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:51.440
You seem awfully sure of yourself.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:52.890
I know, right?

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:56.670
Still, you aren't a resident of the island.

00:04:56.670 --> 00:05:00.820
That's more than enough 
reason not to let you stay.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.450
You guys are pretty insular.

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:05.240
We have our reasons.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:07.500
Anyway, you can keep those clothes.

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.490
Thanks, I appreciate it.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:12.200
Kanejou-san, sorry for calling 
you out so suddenly.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:15.860
Nah, I can't refuse an order from the mayor.

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:23.760
Okay, this boat...

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:29.180
This is Harisu, over.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:30.570
<i>Urgent report from the mayor.</i>

00:05:30.570 --> 00:05:33.840
<i>Daughter missing. Begin search immediately.</i>

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:35.520
What, Karen-chan?

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:38.790
Understood.

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:48.990
Huh? I seem to remember this.

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:00.060
It's the same!

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:01.290
So that means...

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:02.750
Maybe I'm supposed to...

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:19.260
H-Hey, don't scream, idiot!

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:21.170
You're the one who—

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:22.060
Long time no see.

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:25.950
Who do you think you are,
sneaking onto someone's cruiser?!

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:30.240
And what were you about to do, 
you castaway nudist pervert?!

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:31.840
Oh, sorry.

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:35.280
I thought I could predict the 
future, but I was wrong.

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:38.140
It's not something to laugh about!

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:40.050
I'm seriously very sorry.

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:43.000
If it'll help, you can punch or kick 
me to your heart's content.

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:46.170
I-I wouldn't want to go that far.

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:47.990
Karen, are you in there?

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:48.630
It's my dad.

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:50.150
Your dad?

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:52.850
This is all your fault!

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:55.470
I was going to use this 
boat to finally be free.

00:06:56.860 --> 00:06:58.480
You.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:01.350
You're the drifter, aren't you?

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:02.890
What have you done to my daughter?!

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:04.280
If it's anything untoward...

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:07.780
No, Dad! He didn't get a 
chance to do anything!

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:08.960
"Didn't get a chance"?

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:12.290
So one wrong move and you would 
have tarnished my daughter?!

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:13.780
You're so annoying!

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:15.290
Wait, Karen!

00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:19.010
Hey, wait!

00:07:19.010 --> 00:07:20.270
Karen-chan?

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:21.920
What are you waiting for?

00:07:22.230 --> 00:07:23.880
Go catch her!

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:25.170
Huh? But...

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:27.340
No excuses!

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:31.880
I'm not sure what's going on,

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:34.680
but I'm off the hook.

00:07:58.790 --> 00:08:00.180
What d'ya know?

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.750
They're beautiful.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.940
I'm tired.

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:12.060
What song is that?

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:12.060
At this promised place

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:12.060
I keep to my heart

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:37.160
The dreams and hopes that
I want to make come true with you

00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:47.320
No matter how much time passes

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:52.180
The memories will never fade

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:58.880
I'lll search for them
and find them every time

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:08.900
Rinne...

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:14.240
Are you Rinne?

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:17.190
Who are you?

00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:20.900
I'm...

00:09:22.430 --> 00:09:23.540
Setsuna.

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:26.290
Setsuna?

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:31.930
You're Setsuna?

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:35.420
A servant?

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:40.680
Yes, you know how we were looking for 
someone new after Tome-san died, right?

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:42.310
Yeah, you were advertising for someone.

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:44.930
We couldn't find anyone on the island,

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:47.010
so we hired someone from the mainland.

00:09:47.010 --> 00:09:51.980
Then he tripped and fell down the stairs 
on his first day and turned stupid.

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:53.470
So that's how he lost his memory?

00:09:53.470 --> 00:09:56.110
Yes, but he's okay now, right?

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:58.400
Yeah, I remember.

00:09:58.400 --> 00:09:59.900
My name is Setsuna.

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:01.290
Setsuna?

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:02.180
What about your family name?

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:04.330
Um...

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:05.660
Sanzenkai.

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:10.020
For now, we'll call him Sanzenkai Setsuna.

00:10:10.020 --> 00:10:12.500
He hasn't remembered his family name yet.

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:13.800
I see.

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:16.130
Now that that's settled...

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:19.460
I'm Sanzenkai Setsuna.

00:10:19.460 --> 00:10:21.390
Nice to meet you, resident officer.

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:28.290
Hey, do we know each other?

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:29.570
I don't know.

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:32.770
But you asked if I was Setsuna.

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:34.520
I know Setsuna,

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:37.780
but I don't know whether you're him or not.

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:42.070
Be careful.

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:44.280
That's a Qing vase worth 15,000,000.

00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:45.530
Cruzeiros?

00:10:45.530 --> 00:10:46.380
Pounds.

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:47.600
Really?

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:48.690
I don't know.

00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:53.510
You're really rich.

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:56.090
No matter how old it is, it's one of 
Urashima's three wealthiest families.

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:57.090
Urashima?

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:59.070
The name of this island.

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:02.480
More importantly, is it true that you 
traveled through time to get here?

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:05.200
Yeah, I remember that clearly, at least.

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:07.050
I'm a time traveler.

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:17.400
You don't have to believe me, but it's true.

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:20.240
I believe you.

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:23.240
R-Really?

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:25.490
After all, I'm one, too.

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:29.540
I was found in the sea five years ago.

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:31.420
I don't remember anything before that.

00:11:32.450 --> 00:11:34.420
You, too?

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:38.170
So let's look for what you lost, together.

00:11:39.490 --> 00:11:43.440
Mom, the new maid is here.

00:11:46.170 --> 00:11:49.050
Hi, I'm the new maid, Sanzenkai Setsuna.

00:11:49.050 --> 00:11:49.520
Nice to meet you.

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:50.890
<b>Setsuna?</b>

00:11:51.090 --> 00:11:52.880
Yes, Setsuna.

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:54.870
But you can call him Sanzenkai.

00:11:54.870 --> 00:11:55.520
"But"?

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:57.360
<b>He's rather forward for a maid!</b>

00:11:58.630 --> 00:11:59.860
<b>But I like him.</b>

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:03.360
<b>I'm Ohara Kuon. Nice to meet you.</b>

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:16.520
This is your room.

00:12:16.520 --> 00:12:18.170
Let me know if you need anything.

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:20.470
There's actually more than enough here.

00:12:20.470 --> 00:12:22.990
Okay. Get ready to work tomorrow.

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:28.760
I guess this works.

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:16.810
I will kill Setsuna. I swear!

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:32.940
H-Hey, what's up?

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:35.470
Is it morning?

00:13:35.470 --> 00:13:38.060
Why were you sleeping here?

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:39.080
Are you in love with me?

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:41.360
Y-You idiot!

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:45.420
I was keeping watch in case you tried 
to steal something and run off!

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:50.100
The position you were in suggested 
you were watching me sleep.

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:52.090
Don't be so full of yourself!

00:13:52.090 --> 00:13:54.470
Hurry up out of bed and get to work!

00:13:57.410 --> 00:14:00.490
You're okay with toast, a sunny-side-up 
egg and cup of soup, right?

00:14:00.490 --> 00:14:02.880
I'll pass. I'm going to bed.

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:04.960
Huh? You're going to sleep again?

00:14:04.960 --> 00:14:07.040
That was just a catnap.

00:14:07.040 --> 00:14:07.860
Good night.

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:08.940
Hey!

00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:11.490
Hey.

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:15.580
Who might you be?

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:17.580
Sara-chan.

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:21.360
I'm the head of the Urashima 
Shrine, Garandou Sara.

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:23.520
I heard about you from Karen.

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:28.060
Are you the wise, powerful, and 
brave boy from a future land?

00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:30.340
News sure travels fast.

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:32.350
It's true, then?

00:14:32.820 --> 00:14:34.560
Well, yeah.

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:40.120
I must tell you something. Come with me!

00:14:40.120 --> 00:14:42.060
Huh? But I have to...

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:45.440
It's an important tale about 
your fate for crossing time!

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:50.410
Wait!

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:58.910
<b>Urashima Library</b>

00:14:57.250 --> 00:14:58.910
This is my house and...

00:14:59.260 --> 00:15:00.710
the Urashima Library and...

00:15:00.930 --> 00:15:03.300
the backup office for 
the Urashima Shrine!

00:15:10.100 --> 00:15:12.040
What is this place?

00:15:12.040 --> 00:15:14.840
It doesn't look like a shrine maiden's room.

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:19.050
You've come from the future 
to change the past.

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:20.850
Isn't that right?

00:15:22.780 --> 00:15:25.020
I don't have any proof, but I think so.

00:15:26.970 --> 00:15:28.780
Do I know you?

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:32.550
No, I've never met you before.

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:33.620
Right.

00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:36.160
Your boobs aren't that big, either.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:39.600
Sexual harassment, sexual harassment, 
sexual harassment!

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:39.600
Ow! I'm sorry!

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:42.540
Just so you know: I'm fine with flat chests.

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:47.670
Do you mean the flower of your love 
has bloomed upon our first meeting?

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:50.650
That's not what I meant! 
I had to say something.

00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:53.120
So tell me why I'm here.

00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:54.340
Oh, right.

00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:58.850
Setsuna-san, I've heard that 
you've lost your memory.

00:15:59.090 --> 00:16:01.820
Yeah, I have just a small portion of it.

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:06.360
Your memory may have been 
intentionally sealed.

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:07.610
What?!

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:09.780
Who would do that?

00:16:10.130 --> 00:16:12.350
I can't tell who.

00:16:12.350 --> 00:16:14.860
But your time travel

00:16:14.860 --> 00:16:20.250
and Rinne's disappearance five
years ago may prove my theory.

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:21.650
Disappearance?

00:16:21.650 --> 00:16:25.240
Both events happened at the same 
time that island appeared.

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:29.130
Once again, a storm has brought 
a mystery along with that island.

00:16:29.410 --> 00:16:31.590
A singularity may have formed,

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:36.140
causing particles to change into 
tachyons and get blown into the past.

00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:37.320
Huh?

00:16:37.320 --> 00:16:39.880
There's no need to go into detail.

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:42.620
It will have been a waste 
in just a few minutes.

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:43.600
What does that mean?

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:44.830
Here's what it means!

00:16:44.830 --> 00:16:46.780
Setsuna-san, prepare to die!

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:54.570
Ow...

00:17:00.260 --> 00:17:01.540
I'm bleeding!

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:04.370
I'm bleeding! I'm bleeding! 
It's red! It's red!

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:09.200
If you hate it that much, 
why'd you try to attack me?

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:13.970
Well, I have a duty to save this island.

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:17.020
You said you liked flat chests, right?

00:17:17.020 --> 00:17:18.180
Huh? Yeah.

00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:22.740
Okay, next time I'll use a 
honey trap to take your life!

00:17:22.740 --> 00:17:25.950
That won't work if you announce it to me.

00:17:25.950 --> 00:17:27.750
Damn it!

00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:30.570
Just get some rest.

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:33.900
Also, this thing doesn't really suit you.

00:17:35.150 --> 00:17:36.110
See ya.

00:17:38.630 --> 00:17:41.340
Why is he being so nice?

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:44.550
I'm supposed to assassinate him.

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:48.880
What's with this island? 
It's full of mysteries.

00:17:49.560 --> 00:17:51.880
And the latest one...

00:17:52.760 --> 00:17:55.880
Where is Rinne's house?!

00:17:57.630 --> 00:18:00.140
Man, what a day.

00:18:00.550 --> 00:18:02.720
And this house is too big!

00:18:03.130 --> 00:18:05.400
Do I have to do this every day?

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:10.230
A basement?

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:20.940
This place...

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:23.490
<b>The Truth of Urashima Legends 
Ohara Norimasa</b>

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:25.140
Ohara?

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:27.710
<b>History of Urashima</b>

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:47.180
<b>Setsuna must die</b>

00:19:17.560 --> 00:19:18.540
Rinne!

00:19:21.150 --> 00:19:22.720
What?

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:24.260
Where are you going?

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:26.350
For my nightly walk.

00:19:26.770 --> 00:19:28.600
Can I come with you?

00:19:28.890 --> 00:19:30.620
Sure, if you want.

00:19:41.560 --> 00:19:42.470
Hey.

00:19:44.220 --> 00:19:47.830
Would you please sing that song again?

00:19:53.470 --> 00:19:54.830
Sure.

00:19:58.280 --> 00:20:04.480
I'm waiting to meet you someday

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:09.120
At this promised place

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:13.540
I keep to my heart

00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:26.480
The dreams and hopes that
I want to make come true with you

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:36.100
No matter how much time passes

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:41.340
The memories will never fade

00:20:41.340 --> 00:20:48.180
I'lll search for them
and find them every time

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:54.520
No matter what our fate may be

00:21:00.440 --> 00:21:01.530
What's wrong?

00:21:01.850 --> 00:21:03.550
Nothing, really.

00:21:08.070 --> 00:21:09.910
Why are you crying?

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:10.980
I don't know.

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:13.790
The tears just keep coming.

00:21:14.600 --> 00:21:17.420
That's strange. I wonder why.

00:21:21.260 --> 00:21:24.540
I feel strange, too.

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:31.880
Setsuna-san, I'm sorry.

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:35.270
Please take care of this world.

00:21:43.440 --> 00:21:44.630
Good morning.

00:21:44.630 --> 00:21:45.700
Yeah.

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:47.820
Open a curtain, will ya?

00:21:47.820 --> 00:21:48.850
It's morning—

00:21:48.850 --> 00:21:50.240
Don't!

00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:54.320
No sunlight.

00:21:56.970 --> 00:21:58.400
If the light touches me...

00:21:59.620 --> 00:22:01.210
I'll die.

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:38.680
<b>I don't want you to feel bad</b>
